From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953-xiaomi-markw: disable Venus

The phone's own Venus firmware is rejected by the driver ("Unsupported
property: 0"), and none ships in linux-firmware for msm8953, so the probe
fails. venus_probe() has turned the core clocks on by then and its error
path never turns them off, so they stay on for the whole boot. They are
fed from the RPM XO clock, and with them on the apps side keeps XO in its
RPM sleep set and the SoC never reaches VDD minimization in s2idle.

Disable the node until there is firmware to run.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
@@ -331,6 +331,14 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&venus {
+	/*
+	 * No Venus firmware this driver accepts ships with the phone, and a
+	 * failed probe leaves the Venus clocks on, which keeps XO running.
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &wcd_codec {
 	/delete-property/ qcom,gnd-jack-type-normally-open;
 	qcom,mbhc-vthreshold-high = <75 225 450 510 540>;
